From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Irene Sanz <irene.sanz@example.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:35:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] chore(lint): read the current time through an injected
 Clock in the backend

Use cases take a Clock (OrderPlacer, ProductReviewCreator) and SystemClock is the only adapter that reads the system time. A local ESLint plugin hosts the rule, since no-restricted-syntax already serves another convention on these files. DomainEvent is the baseline in eslint-suppressions.json.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code - Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
